#: ../../topics/preview.rst:5
msgid "Preview streaming"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:7
msgid ""
"Preview streaming lets a requester see the text of a reply while the "
"provider is still writing it. This page describes how a provider enables "
"previews, how a requester asks for them, which limits apply to a preview,"
" and why a preview is not a result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:17
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:19
msgid ""
"A provider that answers a text task with a language model can take a long"
" time to finish. Without previews the requester sees nothing until the "
"result arrives. With previews the provider sends a snapshot of the reply "
"at intervals. The requester sees the end of the text so far and can tell "
"whether the task is progressing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:25
msgid ""
"A preview is not part of the task. It is not stored, it does not appear "
"in the history of the task, and it is not signed as a result. The result "
"that ends the task replaces every preview, and the result is the only "
"text that the receipt covers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:30
msgid "Previews are off by default. Both sides take part:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:32
msgid ""
"the provider enables previews on its node, and a text task is the only "
"kind of task that can be previewed;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:34
msgid ""
"the requester asks for previews for each task. A requester that does not "
"ask receives none."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:38
msgid "Enabling previews on a provider"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:40
msgid "The setting ``stream_preview`` takes three values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:42
msgid "``off``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:43
msgid "The default. The node sends no preview."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:45
msgid "``on``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:46
msgid "The node sends previews to requesters that ask for them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:48
msgid "``with_reasoning``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:49
msgid ""
"As ``on``, and the node also sends the reasoning text of the model to "
"requesters that ask for it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:52
msgid "The ``anet preview`` command shows and changes the setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:60
msgid ""
"Setting ``with_reasoning`` asks for confirmation on a terminal, because "
"the reasoning of a model can contain the system prompt and internal "
"information. The other values do not ask for confirmation. Changing "
"between ``off`` and the other values causes the node to publish its card "
"again, so that requesters can see whether the provider sends previews "
"(see :doc:`capabilities`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:80
msgid "Sources of preview text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:82
msgid ""
"A node sends a preview only when something supplies the text so far. "
"There are two sources."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:85
msgid "The ``openai`` auto-reply backend"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:86
msgid ""
"When the task asks for previews, the daemon calls the model service in "
"streaming mode, collects the text as it arrives, and hands it to the "
"preview sender. The final reply is identical, byte for byte, to the reply"
" of a non-streaming call. If a streaming call fails, the node does not "
"repeat it as a non-streaming call, because that would be billed twice."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:92
msgid "The control interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:93
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A program that the operator runs can push the text written so far to "
"``POST /tasks/preview`` on the local control interface. The request body "
"is ``{\"task_id\": \"...\", \"text\": \"...\", \"reasoning\": \"...\"}``,"
" where ``text`` is at most 1 MiB and ``reasoning`` is optional. The call "
"needs the control token. A successful call returns ``{\"sent\": true}``, "
"which means that the text was handed to the sender, not that it arrived."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:100
msgid "``POST /tasks/preview`` answers with these refusals:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:102
msgid "``preview_off`` (409)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:103
msgid "Previews are off on this node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:105
msgid "``task_not_open`` (409)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:106
msgid "The task has ended or is not a text task sent to this node."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:108
msgid "``not_requested`` (200 with ``\"sent\": false``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:109
msgid "The requester did not ask for a preview in this turn."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:111
msgid ""
"The following command pushes a text for the default identity. It reads "
"the control address from ``config.json`` and the token from "
"``control_token.txt`` in the data directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:124
msgid "The ``exec`` backend of auto-reply does not supply preview text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:132
msgid "Asking for previews as a requester"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:134
msgid "A requester asks for previews for a single task."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:136
msgid "Command line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:137
msgid ""
"``anet delegate <aid> \"text\" --watch`` sends the task, asks for "
"previews and continues with ``anet task watch``. ``anet task watch <task-"
"id>`` follows a task that already exists and prints previews, delivery "
"state changes and the final result. The option ``--reasoning`` prints the"
" reasoning text when the provider sends it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:143
msgid "Local A2A interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:144
msgid ""
"A client that streams a message with ``SendStreamingMessage`` or follows "
"a task with ``SubscribeToTask``, and that has activated the extension "
"``https://agentnetwork.org.cn/a2a/ext/anet-preview/v1``, receives each "
"preview as an update of the artifact ``anet.reply``. The update replaces "
"the previous text of the artifact and is marked with ``anet.preview: "
"true`` in its metadata. When the preview omits the beginning of the text,"
" it starts with an ellipsis. A client that has not activated the "
"extension receives no preview event."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:153
msgid "MCP"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:154
msgid ""
"MCP does not expose previews. ``wait_task`` returns the task when its "
"state changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:168
msgid "``anet card <aid>`` shows a line when the provider declares previews."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:178
msgid "Limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:180
msgid "The values are fixed in the code and have no setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:186
msgid "Limit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:187
msgid "Value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:188
msgid "Interval between two previews of one task"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:189
msgid "at least 5 seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:190
msgid "Delay of the last change"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:191
msgid "sent within 5 seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:192
msgid "Previews sent by one node"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:193
msgid "at most 20 per second; the rest are dropped and counted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:194
msgid "Text of a preview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:195
msgid "the last 8 KiB, cut at a character boundary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:196
msgid "Lifetime of a preview in transit"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:197
msgid "60 seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:198
msgid "Previews accepted for one task"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:199
msgid "one per 2 seconds"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:200
msgid "Previews accepted from one peer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:201
msgid "10 per second"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:202
msgid "Tasks whose latest preview is kept by a requester"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:203
msgid "1024"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:205
msgid ""
"A preview is sent only while the task is open and while the provider has "
"not yet sent an answer for the current turn. When the real answer or "
"result is queued, the node cancels the previews that are still waiting, "
"and no preview of that turn is sent afterwards. A requester accepts a "
"preview only if it is for a task that it sent, is newer than the previews"
" it has seen, and answers the message that asked for it. A preview that "
"fails these checks is discarded without a reply."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:214
msgid "Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:216
msgid ""
"A preview is sent as an ordinary encrypted message through the hub, "
"signed by the provider. The hub cannot read it. The message carries a "
"short lifetime of 60 seconds, and a hub discards it when the lifetime "
"ends."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:219
msgid ""
"A preview is held in memory only. It is not written to the task database,"
" the outbound queue or the evidence chain, and its text is not written to"
" a log."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:221
msgid ""
"A requester keeps only the latest preview of each task. A new message or "
"the result of the task, and the end of the task, delete it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:223
msgid ""
"A restart of the provider forgets the turn that was being previewed. That"
" turn sends no further previews and its result is delivered as usual. The"
" next turn can be previewed again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:226
msgid ""
"``GetTask``, the task history and every MCP tool never contain a preview."
" The reasoning text appears only on the local control interface and is "
"never in the local A2A projection."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:231
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:233
msgid ""
"A preview can differ from the final reply. A model can write a text and "
"then replace it. Any program that displays previews must label them as "
"previews, and must not act on them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:236
msgid ""
"Reasoning previews can reveal the instructions and internal data of the "
"provider. They are off by default and need a separate confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:238
msgid ""
"A peer that holds an earlier key of the provider, and that has not yet "
"learned of a key rotation, can forge a preview for a task in progress. "
"Previews are verified against the identity record stored for the peer and"
" do not require a fresh key confirmation. A forged preview is never "
"stored and is replaced by the result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../topics/preview.rst:243
msgid ""
"A provider whose node has previews on and no ``openai`` backend sends "
"previews only through ``POST /tasks/preview``. ``anet doctor`` reports "
"this as information."
msgstr ""

